# Control arms and measurement worktrees. AGENTS.md requires they live here
# rather than beside the repository, where nothing can see them.
.claude/worktrees/

# The sentence models the two no-model tiers run on, and the runtime that
# executes them. Fetched once by `npm run models:fetch`, never committed:
# this repository is a fork, and a fork on GitHub cannot hold its own large
# files - they would have to live in the upstream repository, which is not
# ours to write to. `models/README.md` says what each file is and records
# the sweep that chose these two.
models/**/*.onnx
models/**/vocab.txt
models/**/config.json
models/**/tokenizer_config.json
web/tier/**/*.onnx
web/tier/**/vocab.txt
web/tier/ort/
*.f32
models/**/verb-corpus.json
web/tier/**/verb-corpus.json

# The local launcher and the run it saves. Ports, model names and database
# paths are per-machine, and a committed launcher becomes somebody else's
# ports. `README.md` says what it does and how to write your own if it is not
# in your checkout.
#
# Every spelling of it, because the launcher is the file people rewrite: a
# .cmd or .bat wrapper is the usual second attempt when a .ps1 will not run,
# and it would be the one thing here that is not ignored.
play.ps1
play.cmd
play.bat
play.db
play.db-shm
play.db-wal

# Benchmark output for review. Regenerated by scripts/a-xianxia-run.ts.
llm-results/
xianxia-run-*.txt
intent-trace-*.txt
